Error [jet.ComptimeValueIsComputedFunction]: This compile-time value is a `fn(Int) -> Int` that running code made, a function with no data form
  --> Tests/UI/comptime_dependency_closure_value.jet:7:12
    |
  7 | ADD3: #run adder(3)
    |            ^^^^^
 Why: A compile-time value must be data, which the build keeps and hands to the program. The build keeps a function only when the value names it, as in `F: double`. A function that a call returns, such as a closure, belongs to the run that made it.
 Fix: Name the function in the value (`F: double`), or keep the data the function needs as the compile-time value and pass it to a named function.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E1020
